  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The PI wants the leave-one-out co-expression network for sample R17 in a 45-sample root microbiome expression cohort. Can LIONESS-COEXPRESSION retain its sample identity and keep that result separate from the aggregate?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"the leave-one-out co-expression network for sample R17 in a 45-sample root microbiome expression cohort\" -- available from LIONESS-COEXPRESSION.\n2. \"Can LIONESS-COEXPRESSION retain its sample identity and keep that result separate from the aggregate?\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set. LIONESS-COEXPRESSION gives: one gene-gene co-expression network per sample, plus the aggregate.\n\nSeveral registered methods fit this result; they differ in their modeling assumptions:\n\n- **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** — LIONESS represents the cohort network through sample contributions: W_q = N*W_all - (N-1)*W_without_q, where N is the cohort size and the same base estimator is fitted with and without sample q. Needs expression matrix.\n- **COBRA** — COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Needs expression matrix and sample covariate design matrix.\n- **BONOBO** — BONOBO applies Bayesian estimation and shrinkage to sample-specific gene-gene co-expression. Needs expression matrix.\n\nShould the result be aggregate or sample-specific?\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
